{"rows": [
{"n": 1, "label": "requested", "why": "Only decides how the requested page works and looks: \"GET / serves a playable HTML page titled \"Checkers\" with an 8x8 board where two players take turns on the same page\"."},
{"n": 2, "label": "requested", "why": "\"POST /api/move ... returns JSON with \"ok\" true or false, \"turn\" set to \"red\" or \"black\", and \"winner\" null or the winning colour. An illegal move returns \"ok\": false and leaves the turn unchanged\"."},
{"n": 3, "label": "requested", "why": "Decides how the requested games are held: \"GET /api/new starts a game and returns JSON with a game id\"."},
{"n": 4, "label": "implied", "why": "Requests arriving close together must apply in order, or the rule that \"a legal move switches the turn\" could corrupt game state, and the single-threaded event loop provides that ordering with no extra machinery."},
{"n": 5, "label": "implied", "why": "POST /api/move must reject malformed or oversized JSON bodies, or the server could crash or hang and the requested move endpoint would fail."},
{"n": 6, "label": "requested", "why": "\"server.js starts the server on the port in the PORT environment variable (default 3000)\"."},
{"n": 7, "label": "implied", "why": "Visible focus and labelled squares are accessibility rigour on the requested \"playable HTML page\" board, so players can operate and read it."}
]}
